# Language Standards for AI Engineering Projects

## Code & Comments
- **ALL code MUST be in English**: variable names, function names, class names
- **ALL comments MUST be in English**: inline comments, docstrings, TODO comments
- **ALL documentation MUST be in English**: README, docs/, commit messages

## Rationale
- Portfolio/GitHub projects for international audience
- Collaboration with global teams
- LLM context is trained predominantly on English code
- Consistency with open-source ecosystem

## Docstrings
- Use Google-style or NumPy-style docstrings (choose one)
- Always include: brief description, Args, Returns, Raises (if applicable)
- For AI tools/agents: document expected LLM behavior and edge cases

## Examples
✅ Good:
```python
def generate_embeddings(chunks: list[str]) -> list[np.ndarray]:
    """Generates vector embeddings for text chunks using Vertex AI.
    
    Args:
        chunks: List of text strings to embed
        
    Returns:
        List of embedding vectors as numpy arrays
        
    Raises:
        APIError: If Vertex AI API call fails
    """
```

❌ Bad:
```python
def generar_embeddings(chunks: list[str]) -> list[np.ndarray]:
    """Genera embeddings para chunks de texto"""  # Spanish!
    # Llamar al modelo  # Spanish comment!
```

## Enforcement
- Run linters/pre-commit hooks to catch non-English identifiers
- Review all docstrings before committing